> I am aware that there are several robust options (MLM, MLMVS, MLMV, MLF, MLR) available for the estimators, but I'm not sure which one to use and how to make that decision. Could anyone give me some guidelines, please?

I usually default to MLR because it is the most general, in that it can be applied when there are missing data and you want to use FIML.  Even with complete data, it is asymptotically equivalent to MLM, which may be preferable in smaller samples with no missing data.

Since this is not lavaan-specific, you can post your question on SEMNET <http://www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html> if you want more information about the adjustments.

