Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> Would you have any advice?

If they are exogenous variables, you don't need to model their correlation, you can just calculate it using a polychoric correlation estimator (e.g., lavCor(), or polychoric() from the psych package).

If you want to do the pseudo-latent variable method, you need to make those your regressors, don't keep using the "indicators" as regressors.  And you should probably move the regressands into the latent space, too (that's what lavaan would have to do behind the curtain anyway to estimate those regression paths).

Terrence D. Jorgensen
