Hi,

I am quite new to fitting models with categorial variables and therefor would really appreciate some help.

I ran a model with a binary endogenous variable and the results look suspicious to me.

Here is the code I used:

KINDEP2 <- '#measurement model
            PE =~ apk1 + apk2 + apk6 + apk9 + apk13 + apk16 + apk23 + apk25 + apk29 + apk33
                  + apk34 + apk37 + apk40 + apk42 + apk45 + apk47 + apk49
            DEP =~ deq02 + deq19 + deq23 + deq50 + deq55
            SC =~ deq07 + deq13 + deq30 + deq36 + deq53 + deq64 + deq66

            #structural model
            DEP ~ PE
            SC ~ PE
            Gruppe ~ DEP + SC + PE

            #cov
            DEP ~~ SC
            '

fit <- sem(KINDEP2, data = KINDEP, ordered = "Gruppe")
summary(fit, standardized = TRUE)
fitMeasures(fit, c("cfi", "rmsea", "srmr"))

My console prints this (please see below):

- How is it possible to get a p-value of 1?
- How is it possible to get a CFI estimation of 1 and RMSEA = 0, while SRMR seems to provide a reasonable estimation?
- Also: can anybody recommend a book or paper on fitting categorial models in SEM?

Thanks a lot in advance!
Best,
Simone

