> - How is it possible to get a p-value of 1?

p values can approach (i.e., round up to) 1 when most of the sampling distribution is more extreme than the observed statistic.

> - How is it possible to get a CFI estimation of 1 and RMSEA = 0, while SRMR seems to provide a reasonable estimation?

You want to pay attention to the "robust" column.  The corresponding chi-squared-based fit indices have a ".scaled" suffix.
> fitMeasures(fit, c("cfi.scaled", "rmsea.scaled", "srmr"))

> - Also: can anybody recommend a book or paper on fitting categorial models in SEM?

Hoyle's (2012) Handbook of Structural Equation Modeling has a couple chapters dealing with categorical endogenous variables.  Here is a Jöreskog paper you might find helpful:

http://dx.doi.org/10.1207/S15327906347-387

You can also post general SEM questions like this on SEMNET:

www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html <http://www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html>

