> Would anyone be able to advise me on how to get the confidence intervals for these correlation coefficients?

That output is just the standardized model-implied covariance matrix among common factors.  You can get SEs from the standardizedSolution() output, but I wouldn't construct normal-theory CIs from them because standardized parameters have boundaries that the CI might cross.  If you set the argument "std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE" to identify the latent scale by fixing factor variances to 1, then your estimated covariances are correlations, so you can use those confidence intervals from summary(fit, ci = TRUE) or parameterEstimates(fit).

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
UvA web page: http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

